  "result": "Perfect! All 166 tests pass. I've successfully added voucher support to invoices:\n\n**New functionality in `src/invoices.js`:**\n\n1. **`applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount })`** \u2014 Applies a fixed-amount discount voucher\n   - Takes a fixed amount in cents off the invoice (after VAT)\n   - Returns `ok(newInvoice)` with `invoice.voucher = { code, amount }`\n   - Errors:\n     - `NOT_DRAFT`: Invoice must be draft status\n     - `VOUCHER_EXISTS`: Only one voucher per invoice\n     - `AMOUNT_INVALID`: Amount must be a positive integer\n   - Never mutates original invoice\n\n2. **Updated `invoiceTotals()`** now returns:\n   ```javascript\n   {\n     subtotal,    // sum of line totals\n     discount,    // sum of line discounts\n     vat,         // sum of line VATs\n     voucher,     // voucher amount (0 if no voucher)\n     total        // subtotal - discount + vat - voucher (clamped to 0 min)\n   }\n   ```\n\n3. **New error code:**\n   - `VOUCHER_EXISTS`: Cannot apply multiple vouchers to one invoice\n\n**Test coverage includes:**\n- Applying vouchers to draft invoices\n- Rejecting vouchers on non-draft invoices\n- Preventing multiple vouchers on same invoice\n- Amount validation (zero, negative, fractional amounts)\n- Total calculation with vouchers\n- Mutation safety\n- Edge cases (voucher exceeding total)\n\nVouchers now provide a clean way to apply fixed-amount promotional discounts to invoices. \u2714",
